Rule: 'A candidate that parses as strict JSON, or as JSON with repeated keys resolved last-wins, is scoreable' and 'The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one'. For the input fence[ A ] with A = {"a":1,"a":2}, the fenced object A is scoreable by the repeated-keys last-wins clause, so recovery returns A. For the rewritten fence[ A ] B, the same fenced object A is still the last one inside a code fence and is scoreable, so recovery still returns A. Therefore the rule says unchanged.